[CENTER][SIZE=5][B]🚇 1.0.0.3 — Lines with both directions[/B][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdreval/MTR-Dynmap-Bridge/main/docs/images/web-map-lines-merged.jpg[/IMG][/CENTER]

In MTR a line is usually two routes — there and back. The web map used to list them separately, so every line appeared twice. Now both directions are [B]one line[/B], like on MTR's own system map.

[LIST]
[*][B]☑️ Merge directions[/B] — new tick in the Lines list. Routes with the same number become one line (without a number: same name and colour). On by default, each browser remembers the choice.
[*][B]🎨 Highlight a whole line[/B] — click it to highlight both directions; the rest of the network fades out and the vehicle list shows only that line.
[*][B]▸ Directions[/B] — open a line to see A1 → A2 and A2 → A1 and highlight just one of them. Circular lines show clockwise / anticlockwise.
[*][B]🧾 Station window by direction[/B] — vehicles at the station and on their way, split by line and direction, with distance and speed.
[*]Untick Merge directions to get the old list with every route on its own row.
[/LIST]

[B]Upgrade:[/B] replace the jar with 1.0.0.3 and restart the server — config.yml does not change. Reload the web map with Ctrl + F5.
